    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$60\\text{ m}$ or $101.26\\text{ m}$. Cut to an opposite-side midpoint and rotate the small triangle through $180^\\circ$. The resulting perpendicular sides are $24\\text{ m}$ and $10\\text{ m}$, or $48\\text{ m}$ and $5\\text{ m}$; use Pythagoras’ theorem and add the three sides.",
      "worked": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "ba871a67-bc58-4569-a1fd-7dcb555f8671",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Cut from a corner to the midpoint of an opposite side. There are two possibilities. In each case, rotate the small triangle through ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "180^\\circ",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " about that midpoint and join it to the trapezium. The two equal sloping edges form the hypotenuse of the large triangle.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "2523253f-1232-4443-80f0-330e980a02a6",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "If the cut ends at the midpoint of a 24 m side, the small triangle has perpendicular sides 12 m and 5 m. The rearranged triangle has perpendicular sides 24 m and 10 m.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "0841d248-147f-41eb-a397-753779ad937f",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{align*}h_1&=\\sqrt{24^2+10^2}\\\\h_1&=\\sqrt{676}\\\\h_1&=26\\text{ m}\\\\P_1&=24+10+26\\\\P_1&=60\\text{ m}\\end{align*}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "2945ea10-3d68-4bd5-b86c-b0b0a2ea74ec",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "If the cut ends at the midpoint of a 5 m side, the small triangle has perpendicular sides 24 m and 2.5 m. The rearranged triangle has perpendicular sides 48 m and 5 m.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f6125038-3222-4d5d-9bee-61aba22a6308",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{align*}h_2&=\\sqrt{48^2+5^2}\\\\h_2&=\\sqrt{2329}\\text{ m}\\\\P_2&=48+5+\\sqrt{2329}\\\\P_2&=53+\\sqrt{2329}\\text{ m}\\\\P_2&\\approx101.26\\text{ m}\\end{align*}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "c6f6b8b7-8941-4e35-a300-69d119494ccc",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Both constructions preserve the original area:",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ce0de7f9-517b-4ed5-af3e-cc341bd185cc",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{rectangle}}&=5\\times24=120\\text{ m}^2\\\\A_1&=\\tfrac12\\times24\\times10=120\\text{ m}^2\\\\A_2&=\\tfrac12\\times48\\times5=120\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
